Description: cap the frame rate to 60 frames per second
 The intro has no timer: the animation (k += .005) and the scroll text
 advance by a fixed step on each frame, while the music is driven by the
 audio callback. On current hardware the effect runs far too fast and out
 of sync with the music. Wait with SDL_Delay() so that frames are drawn at
 BUGY_FPS (60 by default, can be changed with -DBUGY_FPS=n). The schedule is
 based on the frame count, so it does not drift; it is reset when the
 machine is more than 100 ms late.
